  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_inception_module(x: list, W1: list, W3: list, W5: list, W_pool: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Inception Module** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_inception_module(x: list, W1: list, W3: list, W5: list, W_pool: list) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(x, dtype=float)\n    branches = [arr @ np.array(W, dtype=float) for W in [W1, W3, W5, W_pool]]\n    return np.round(np.concatenate(branches, axis=-1), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
